## A native library for another machine is an error (ImplementationPlan.md
## 5.10.8 'machine and class checked against the triple', 5.10.14; recon p2
## native-imports 8.5):
##   <path>: ELF machine <EM_x> does not match target <triple>
## and the COFF and PE forms for import libraries and DLLs (whose exact
## wording the plan leaves open: the file, the word 'machine' and the
## target are pinned). A P/Invoke into a library of another machine could
## never load. The same libraries link for their own machine: aarch64 MSIL
## triples bind EM_AARCH64 shared objects and ARM64 import libraries, as
## x86_64 ones bind EM_X86_64 and AMD64 ones.
## The ELF class and data encoding are checked too:
##   <path>: ELF machine <EM_x> (ELFCLASS32) does not match target <triple>
##   <path>: ELF machine <EM_x> (ELFDATA2MSB) does not match target <triple>
## A native library is read only in the object format of the triple's OS
## (the section 12 row of 2026-10-23 for 5.10.8-5.10.14): ELF on Linux,
## PE/COFF on Windows. A file of the other format given on the command line
## or by -l:<file> is
##   <path>: ELF file cannot be imported for target <triple>
## on windows-msvc and windows-gnu (lld-link rejects an ELF input), and
##   <path>: PE/COFF file cannot be imported for target <triple>
## on Linux (an import library, a native DLL, a MinGW import library), never
## a P/Invoke that fails at run time.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/native/libfoo.yaml -o x64.so
# RUN: yaml2obj -D MACHINE=EM_AARCH64 %S/Inputs/native/libfoo.yaml -o a64.so
# RUN: yaml2obj -D CLASS=ELFCLASS32 -D MACHINE=EM_386 %S/Inputs/native/libfoo.yaml -o i386.so
# RUN: llvm-lib /machine:x64 /def:foo.def /out:x64.lib
# RUN: llvm-lib /machine:arm64 /def:foo.def /out:arm64.lib
# RUN: yaml2obj -D FN1=foo -D MACHINE=IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_ARM64 %S/Inputs/native/coff-code.yaml -o arm64.obj
## lld-link's own import library would overwrite arm64.lib (LIBRARY foo.dll).
